A mapping that reads a key only a pattern constraint matches. Only a field
with a predictable name is declared (docs/translation.md, A4), so a lens reads
no key under a pattern by name.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
Schema: {
	labels: [string]: string
}
-- ship/1.0.thema --
Schema: {
	labels: [string]: string
	env:    string
}

ForwardLens: {
	v0_0: _
	v1_0: {
		env: _coalesce(v0_0.labels.env, "none")
	}
}
-- out/error --
error[E0340]: 0.0 does not declare labels.env
 --> 1.0.thema:9:8
  |
9 |         env: _coalesce(v0_0.labels.env, "none")
  |              ^^^^^^^^^
  |
  = note: only a pattern constraint of 0.0 matches labels.env, and a pattern constraint declares no field
  = help: a lens reads only fields declared by name: declare labels.env as an optional field in a new minor version, for the values instances carry there to land in, then map from it in the lens from that version
